               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_0655607d">34 x 25</dimensions>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_cb730a4d">Written in brown ink. Paper: 14 staves. On the title page in upper left-hand corner: "654. P." being the archive number of The Royal Theatre. In upper right-hand corner added in pencil in foreign hand: "I.C.G. Juul." Above the music on p. 3: "Til 'En Episode' femte Act. Musiken begynder efter Evalds Replik: 'ak, men Lykken raader for Livets Kaar, det er saa Skjæbnens Villie!". On p. 3 after the double bar: "<rend xml:id="idm36" rend="line-through">see Partituret af Fiskerne fra § til §,</rend> derpaa videre næste Side." At the end of the music on p. 11, signed and dated: "I:P:E:H: 30/8 52."</physMedium>
